ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":144,"prev":146,"next":148,"titles":150,"firmware":62},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":10,"order":11,"path":12,"context":13,"summary":18,"status":19,"firmware":20,"facts":26,"procedures":87,"parameters":88,"related":121,"body":124,"sources":125,"official_url":30,"controls":138},"sampler.drum-key-settings","Drum sampler key settings",[5,6,7,8,9],"drum play mode","mute group","choke","drum pan","sample fade","sampler",35,"knowledge/manual/units/sampler/drum-key-settings.md",{"modes":14,"screens":16},[15],"instrument",[17],"M1","The drum sampler's `M1` page shapes the selected key — tune, start, end and play mode, with direction, pan, fade and gain on the shift layer.","current",{"min":21,"changed_in":22,"guide_version":24,"verified_on":25},"1.0.9",[23,24],"1.0.45","1.1.15",null,[27,32,35,40,44,49,53,58,64,67,70,73,77,81,84],{"id":28,"text":29,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"per-key","The settings belong to the selected key, so every key keeps its own values.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/sample#drum-sampler","official",{"id":33,"text":34,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"play-modes","Key plays only while held, oneshot always to the end, mute group is cut off by another mute-group key, loop repeats.",{"id":36,"text":37,"source":38,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":39},"one-group","A kit has a single mute group, so all mute-group keys choke each other — handy for open and closed hats.","docs/research/30-presets-samples.md#27-region-fields-by-type","community",{"id":41,"text":42,"source":43,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"choke-live","The mute group applies across live and sequenced notes alike.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.0.45",{"id":45,"text":46,"source":47,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":48},"ranges","Pan runs from −100 to +100, sample fade from 0 to 99, sample gain from −30 to +20 dB.","docs/research/30-presets-samples.md#26-regions-how-each-field-reaches-the-device-decoded","community-verified",{"id":50,"text":51,"source":52,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"fade-drawn","The screen draws the sample fade over the waveform.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.15",{"id":54,"text":55,"source":56,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":57},"guide-errors","The guide's texts for pan and sample fade describe tune and loop crossfade — copied from the synth sampler by mistake.","docs/research/40-official-docs.md#53-te-errata-we-keep-verbatim-and-our-manual-must-not-copy","derived",{"id":59,"text":60,"source":61,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":62,"confidence":63},"screen","The page shows the selected key's waveform with the skipped parts tinted blue and start and end markers; tune reads as a note symbol and a signed value such as −16.10, moving in steps of 0.1, and play mode as one of four icons — an arrow to a bar, a plain arrow, an arrow with G, or a loop.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#25-engine-pages-instrument-m1","1.1.33","verified",{"id":65,"text":66,"source":61,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":62,"confidence":63},"shift-screen","With `shift` held the page shows direction, pan as a bar from L to R, fade as a dark ramp that rises from the start marker over the wave, and gain, which scales the drawn wave.",{"id":68,"text":69,"source":61,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":62,"confidence":63},"tune-reading","Tune is always signed, so no transposition reads +0.00, and it reaches well past an octave (−16.10 was seen on a key).",{"id":71,"text":72,"source":61,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":62,"confidence":63},"no-cc","CC12–15 on the track's channel move nothing on this page.",{"id":74,"text":75,"source":76,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":62,"confidence":63},"fade-sound","The sample fade is a fade-in from the start marker lasting a fixed time, about 0.25 s at 50 and 0.95 s at 99, so a short hit at a high fade never reaches full level.","docs/research/60-sound-session.md#5-samplers",{"id":78,"text":79,"source":80,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":39},"fade-out","Shift + click on `E3` turns the sample fade into a fade-out; the screen draws a rising ramp for the fade-in and a falling one for the fade-out, and a click switches between them (two videos, narration \"clicking takes you from one to the other\"). How a fade-out sounds is not measured, and the replica ramps linearly to zero over the last fade seconds.","docs/research/78-overnight-accuracy.md#log",{"id":82,"text":83,"source":80,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":39},"tune-hundredths","With `E1` pushed in, the tune shows its hundredths in brackets, such as +0.[36] (one video).",{"id":85,"text":86,"source":80,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":39},"zoom","A click on E2 or E3 zooms the drum page's wave on the start or end point, as on the synth sampler. The marker sits in the middle and the wave slides under it as you turn (one video, OS 1.x).",[],[89,94,99,103,108,113,116,118],{"screen":17,"encoder":90,"layer":91,"keys":92,"name":93,"range":25,"default":25,"cc":25,"cc_confidence":25,"note":25,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"E1","base","turn E1","tune",{"screen":17,"encoder":95,"layer":91,"keys":96,"name":97,"range":25,"default":25,"cc":25,"cc_confidence":25,"note":98,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"E2","turn E2","sample start","push in for finer steps",{"screen":17,"encoder":100,"layer":91,"keys":101,"name":102,"range":25,"default":25,"cc":25,"cc_confidence":25,"note":25,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"E3","turn E3","sample end",{"screen":17,"encoder":104,"layer":91,"keys":105,"name":106,"range":107,"default":25,"cc":25,"cc_confidence":25,"note":25,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"E4","turn E4","play mode","key / oneshot / mute group / loop",{"s